            <div xml:id="d475-a1">

                <pb facs="0857" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg757"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in Mr. Evarts’s No. 28.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ramsey to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >War Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-06-15"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 15,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith copy
                    of telegram from Colonel Hatch, dated the 7th instant, in regard to the
                    movements of hostile Indians in New Mexico. He states that a large number
                    crossed into Mexico.</p>
                <p>The same is also furnished the Secretary of the Interior.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ALEX. RAMSEY,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of
                        War.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
